From e4f8d57a6bd6ffaa22a9cab446a11c25cf404378 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vadik likholetov <vadikas@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:12:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] KVM: arm64: add Tegra234 SMMUv2 pKVM backend

Add a built-in protected-KVM backend for the mirrored Tegra234 MMU-500 instances. The backend owns the SMMU register apertures at EL2, mirrors host stage-2 identity mappings, provides translated host and guest domains, and retains page-granular tables for the Tegra walk-cache erratum.

Reserve and initialize the Android pKVM IOMMU pool needed by the backend. Keep the normal arm-smmu driver mutually exclusive and leave device handoff fail-closed: the mandatory device reset and Tegra MC stream-ID lock are intentionally not provided by this commit.
